  "verbalization": "Amarolide is linked to HPAC through a multi-step mechanism involving the enzyme MOVP-3, which is targeted by Amarolide. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence scores, with the highest confidence in the direct relationship between Amarolide and MOVP-3, followed by the connection between MOVP-3 and HPAC. The evidence suggests that Amarolide inhibits MOVP-3, which in turn affects HPAC, potentially through a biochemical interaction that is not fully elucidated. The presence of a detailed molecular structure for MOVP-3 in one of the paths adds to the complexity of the mechanism, but the core relationship remains consistent across all paths. The integration of these findings supports a plausible mechanism where Amarolide exerts its effect on HPAC via MOVP-3, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully characterized.",
